WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.375
One click.

00:00:01.475 --> 00:00:03.528
Add to cart. Easy, right?

00:00:04.318 --> 00:00:09.398
But behind that one click, there’s a question, a memory, and a little bit of maths.

00:00:10.415 --> 00:00:11.442
Let’s open it up.

00:00:12.199 --> 00:00:15.956
First, the shop itself. Products fly in from an API.

00:00:16.006 --> 00:00:19.472
Filter them. Sort them. Grid, or list.

00:00:20.081 --> 00:00:24.020
Now pick one. Bar stools. Orange. Just one of them.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:24.934
And… click.

00:00:26.034 --> 00:00:26.978
Freeze.

00:00:27.228 --> 00:00:31.806
Question one. Is it already in the cart? Same item? Same colour?

00:00:31.756 --> 00:00:36.273
Yes? Then only the number grows. No? It gets a row of its own.

00:00:38.131 --> 00:00:41.026
And the cart itself? It’s not on some server.

00:00:40.976 --> 00:00:43.690
It’s right here, in the browser’s own memory.

00:00:44.487 --> 00:00:50.781
So this little badge, and everything after it? Count. Total. All worked out from that memory.

00:00:51.352 --> 00:00:55.163
No real payments here. But the logic? That part is real.
